<title>UK: Telspec up after non-executive appointments.</title>
<headline>Telspec up after non-executive appointments.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in telecoms equipment maker Telspec Plc rose on Tuesday after the market welcomed news that the group had appointed David Ball and John Westhead as non-executive directors.</p>
<p>By 1110 GMT the stock was up five pence, or 3.5 percent, at 147-1/5.</p>
<p>Ball is President and CEO of Nortel Public Carrier Networks Europe, Telspec said in a statement, while Westhead is non-executive Deputy Chairman of Bowthorpe Plc.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
